A||||26||Hank is Here||Ignition Upgrade||||1||
Z||000000||Hank is Here||02-25-2001||02:48 PM||||Okay,  the other day I believe that 88BlackGT (Jeff)  said he added a MSD 6AL ignition control to his car and got 5 mpg more.  Now what the heck does this control, does it replace any part of the stock ignition?  If 5 mpg could be achieved then this sounds good.  Does the control box offer any more power?  Who has these or any ignition upgrades, opinions?    <BR>I did a search and was suprized not to find anything on this topic.  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||TheFiero64||02-25-2001||04:01 PM||||I've just installed the Crane HI-6 in my car and it seems to have a large power increase. I haven't calculated any MPG increase yet.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||02-25-2001||04:13 PM||||Before adding any new parts make sure the existing parts are good. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Shaun41178||02-25-2001||04:24 PM||||If you think you got a big power upgrade from an ignition upgrade and you think you could feel it then the stock parts were not up to par and were probably bad or you have to recalibrate your @ss-meter.  Aftermarket ignitions don't add that much hp if any at all over a good stock operating ignition system.  Biggest gains are around 1-2 hp over a good stock system.  But go get it dynoed to get real numbers to see if you did pick up a good amount.  Its the only way to trully know||||reg||1
Z||000004||Black88GT||02-25-2001||05:49 PM||||Travis (1FST2M6) has a lot of experience with MSD and Crane ignition boxes.  I dunno what search you used but I turned up a bunch of posts, as follows....<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000503-2-000915.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000503-2-000915.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000503-2-001188.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000503-2-001188.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000815-2-002196.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000815-2-002196.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20001206-2-003535.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20001206-2-003535.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20010219-2-004850.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20010219-2-004850.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/006387.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/006387.html</A> <P>Before I bought mine I searched it here, and everyone had me sold!  Not a bad word about it and I can see why.  I also got the part numbers and everything.  I got the MSD coil too and the GM harness to make the install easier...<P>||||reg||14
Z||000005||Hank is Here||02-25-2001||06:47 PM||||Okay, on this one I guess I am looking for fuel efficency over power. My car sucks.......fuel that is.  I just filled up the tank and got about 13 mpg on that tank, this was mainly city driving (87 GT auto).  Now I can reach up to 23.5 mpg on the highway but that is even babying it.  The car seems to run strong, the ignition system is okay as far as I know.  It has new plugs, wires, cap rotor.  I don't know why this car sucks fuel.  I have a 88 Chevy with 2.8 DIS and have gotten over 28 mpg out of it ( even with disconnected TCC), the worst was 17 and that was beating it.  I drive that car harder than the Fiero and get about 22 mpg normally abround town.  Hel my one old jeep with motor designed in the 1940's gets 20 mpg around town.  I guess I am fusterated, the car runs well but has no efficency to it.  So ignition is a place where I think some efficnecy could be saved.  I am thinking of the MSD 6A since I don't plan on adding a whole lot of goodies to the car.  <P>Jeff thanks for those links, it seemes odd to me that I couldn't locate them.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Black88GT||02-25-2001||08:22 PM||||Setting any engine codes?  I'm thinking vacuum leak, EGR valve, or Oxygen sensor.  They are 3 common things that can majorly screw up gas mileage.  However you would most likely set an engine code or notice a high idle atleast.  Do you have a fuel leak possibly?  Try replacing your fuel filter and drop the tank to check for any problems (while your at it might as well do your pump).  Just some ideas....<P>||||reg||3
Z||000007||Hank is Here||02-25-2001||10:39 PM||||Nope no codes, just checked tonight. The O2 sensor I replaced about 3 weeks ago.  I am thinking that this is just the nature of the car to suck gas.  But I would like to increase the milage.  <BR>Jeff, when you upgraded your ignition was that the only upgrade you did at that point?   Was that with the 2.8 or 3.4 in it?  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Black88GT||02-25-2001||11:15 PM||||When I did the MSD it was just the 6AL, the MSD Coil, and 8mm wires.  Noticed about 5mpg increase.  This was the 3.4.  I have noticed the 3.4 was getting better gas mileage to begin with then my old 2.8, but the 3.4 has about 1/20th of the mileage then the 2.8 had.  I am upgrading my fuel system as we speak and I am hoping that will help more because my Fuel Filter is (should say was) BEAT!  13 mpg is too low even for an automatic, maybe its your tire pressure or something.  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Hank is Here||02-25-2001||11:42 PM||||Nope tires are up to par.  I have them up to 37 psi. two psi over max   I am dumbfounded too.  Why did you choose the 6AL over the 6A, I know the differences, but what went into your decision?  What milage do you get now?  Also I replaced my fuel filter like 6 months ago.   I will also admit my idle is up about 1000rpm or so.  The car is otherwise bone stock, and it was maintaned by a Pontiac dealer only before I had it.  I have every record of every oil change and maintiance done to the car since new, nothing seems to stand out.   ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Black88GT||02-26-2001||12:10 AM||||I got the 6AL for the built in rev limiter.  You sure you don't have a vacuum leak?  1000 RPMs is kinda high, not to to high.  Other then that I am all out of ideas?||||reg||1
Z||000011||Carrolles||02-26-2001||07:35 AM||||I believe 1000 rpm is about right for idle.  85SE v-6 4 spd idles there and gets 23 to 24 mpg commuting to work on twisty mountain roads.<P>What temp do you see when the engine has reached normal op temp?  If it is in the 160 range (as you often see with a bad t-stat) the computer may not be operating at it's best point.  It has to warm up to around 180 for this.  If not your mileage will suck.<P>Hope this helps,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000012||Shaun41178||02-26-2001||04:00 PM||||When my 2.8 auto is fully warmed up it idles at about 750-800 rpm when it is in gear.  1000 rpm on a warm engine is too high when it is in gear.  With it in park it should be at about 900 or so.  At least that is what mine is<P>A ignition will not get you up to 20 or so miles per gallon.  it might get you up to about 15 but don't expect some miracle with an ignition upgrade.  Something else is wrong ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Black88GT||02-26-2001||04:15 PM||||Yeah 750 - 800 is what mine idles at too (normal), anything higher isn't right.  Of course when I start mine cold its about 1500 but after about 5 min. of driving its down to normal.  Also like Shaun said an ignition will help but won't get you back to normal.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Formula88||02-26-2001||04:29 PM||||My 88 Formula idles at about 1000, and when I started working on it I found out why: busted EGR tube.  Couldn't tell till I went to pull it out.  Being ever so careful not to break it, then noticing it was already broken! ||||reg||6
Z||000015||theogre||02-26-2001||06:59 PM||||If that's an automatic, did you verify the TC is locking. that will hurt milage if it's not.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Hank is Here||02-26-2001||07:17 PM||||I will check the EGR tube Wednsday.  <BR>As for the TC solenoid I do not know if it is locking. How do I test if it is locking?  I konw what one that does not unlock acts like but don't know about the other away around.  ||||reg||1
Z||000017||1FST2M6||02-27-2001||08:24 AM||||I'll get pics and post them tonite of the MSD 6a on the GT the AL on the SE and the Crane Hi-6S on the SE. the MSD makes more HP @ 3500rpm over the Crane about 2 whole hp! the sound of the car is totally different over 3500 when the MSd switches from multispark to capacitve discharge. adding the crane to my SE only helped about 3hp at 4500 and 5.4lbft at 1800rpm but the torque under the curve matched from 4500+ where the HP pulled from 4500+. the MSD just shifted nearly the same numbbers about 1000rpm lower. <BR>ok if i've lost you...<P>4500rpm no crane 113.5hp 149.2lbft<BR>4500rpm with crane 116.9hp and 154.6<BR>3500rpm MSD 118.7hp and 159.0 <BR>  (((note the 10full lbft of torque from stock to the MSD!!))<BR>with the MSD i changed to NGK (UR5) plugs and Mallory plug wires<P>i'll try and scan these sheets and post them. the ONLY ignition piggy pack unit that i've ever been able to FEEL a difference was an MSD 6BTM on a boosted Civic making 17 more HP at the wheels. the Crane HI-6TR on a Nitrous Mustang making like 20 more hp.<P>I've never had a problem with the Accel coils I've had, the MSD coil or the Crane PS91 i have now. <P>if you get a LINK, Haltech, Electromotive, Zdyne or any other full engine management system you'll be able to tune more HP.. HP you CAN feel and see on a dyno. but you'll still need an MSD box as a sub system to the engine management.<P><BR>just my $.02<P><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg">   <BR> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 02-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000018||1FST2M6||02-27-2001||08:30 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6dyno.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6dyno.jpg</A>    -  finished product (disreguard the red line)    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  i'll scan the others so you can see the differences in the curve shift with the MSD over the Crane both are great systems and they one may work better on your car than mine.. <P>heh.. oh yeah.. i've got a lead foot and i never saw a mileage increase with either ignition box.<BR> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 02-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000019||JC Webb||02-27-2001||02:27 PM||||What coil are you running with the MSD 6A to get those great numbers?||||reg||1
Z||000020||terryk||02-27-2001||03:25 PM||||900 RPM is what the ECM is trying to mantain at idle. The tachs are pretty inaccurate so a scanner or remote tach is needed to verify it, but 900 is what the ECM is shooting for.||||reg||1
Z||000021||1FST2M6||02-28-2001||08:12 AM||||i had an Accell Super coil Part # 5001. for those numbers. if/and when you get an MSD or crane you don't have to run a seperate tach lead... tie the 2 pink wires out of the distributor together same with the white and same with the leads out of the wiring harness and ditch the lame capacitor.. you can ditch the capacitor now too.. a CAP smoothes down the spikes on a battery re-connect and causes more problems than it solves. I'll scan these pics in a few minutes.. i'll have to wait for it to stop raining to get pics of the MSD on the GT.  i'll look through my pics and see if i have any older pics of it.. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000022||mrfixit58||02-28-2001||10:03 AM||||Hanks asks,". How do I test if it is locking? I konw what one that does not unlock acts like but don't know about the other away around."<P>I believe the TC is working properly if you notice your RPMs drop approximatly 200 RPMs once you reach steady highway cruise speed, say 55 MPH. THere may be a more advanced test but this is what I've noticed.<P>If this doesn't seem to be the problem, you should consider taking your car to a shop and have them do a complete diagnostic analysis. Use this information to see if you can fix it yourself. With the amount of money your blowing out your tail pipes, your payback for this $55 service will pay for itself in less than SIX tanks of fuel.<P>Hope this helps,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000023||1FST2M6||02-28-2001||10:16 AM||||get on the highway at 60ish crusing (but not with the cruise on) and with your foot on the gas tap the brake if you RPMS jump up 200ish you TC lock works... just bass ackwards of what 58 said.. and easier to see (i think)<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6-open2.jpg">  you can see teh Accel super coil in front of the Nitrous bottle.. the MSD box is under that.. i'll get better pics of the GT...||||reg||1
Z||000024||1FST2M6||03-02-2001||03:10 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fst-msd1.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fst-msd2.jpg"> <P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fst-rear-tag.jpg"> <P>pics of my MSD installed by my 15 year old (soon to be) brother-in-law. if he can do it anyone can... left with the MSD, the instructions and my office phone number. when i got home from work it was done.. i checked it over to make sure it was done right and handed him the keys.. low-an-behold it works! he also Dyed my tail light lenses. Marhyde plastic dye.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000025||1FST2M6||03-02-2001||03:11 PM||||i'll post pics of the new coil and the heat taped wireing this weekend...<P>--- <BR>oh also note the lack of the useless tach filter.. <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 03-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000026||FieroSEt||03-02-2001||08:39 PM||||So, The 6AL is the one to use in a turbo setup? If yes anyone know a part #??  Thank's  ||||reg||1
